# The image is built from three things and nothing else: the Publisher's npm
# tarball, the toolchain's lockfile, and the files under docker/ it copies. So the
# context starts empty and lets those in by name; .git, node_modules, the tests and
# anything a developer leaves lying around never reach the build.
*
!api-only-publisher.tgz
!docker/entrypoint.sh
!docker/asyncapi-analytics.json
!docker/asyncapi-config/production.json
!docker/toolchain/package.json
!docker/toolchain/package-lock.json
